---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="QR code generator: make a QR code for a link, Wi-Fi or contact card"
  description="Make a QR code for a web address, your Wi-Fi details, or a contact card, and download it as a picture. Made in your browser, nothing is uploaded or tracked."
>
  <h1>QR code generator</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Choose what the code should hold, type the details, and download the picture. The code is
    drawn on this page, so your link or Wi-Fi password never passes through a server, and the
    code carries no tracking of ours.
  </p>

  <div class="sheet">
    <div class="field-grid">
      <div>
        <label for="kind">The code holds</label>
        <select id="kind">
          <option value="url">A web address or text</option>
          <option value="wifi">Wi-Fi name and password</option>
          <option value="vcard">A contact card</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="size">Picture size</label>
        <select id="size">
          <option value="512">512 × 512, for screens</option>
          <option value="1024" selected>1024 × 1024, for print</option>
          <option value="2048">2048 × 2048, for big print</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="fields-url">
      <label for="url">Web address or text</label>
      <input type="text" id="url" value="https://example.com" />
    </div>
    <div id="fields-wifi" hidden>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <div>
          <label for="ssid">Wi-Fi name (SSID)</label>
          <input type="text" id="ssid" placeholder="HomeWiFi" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="wifipass">Wi-Fi password</label>
          <input type="text" id="wifipass" placeholder="password" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="security">Security type</label>
          <select id="security">
            <option value="WPA">WPA or WPA2 (most homes)</option>
            <option value="WEP">WEP (old)</option>
            <option value="nopass">No password</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="fields-vcard" hidden>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <div>
          <label for="vc-name">Full name</label>
          <input type="text" id="vc-name" placeholder="Ahmad Ameen" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="vc-phone">Phone</label>
          <input type="text" id="vc-phone" placeholder="+92 300 0000000" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="vc-email">Email</label>
          <input type="text" id="vc-email" placeholder="name@example.com" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="vc-org">Company (optional)</label>
          <input type="text" id="vc-org" placeholder="" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:1rem;">
      <button class="btn btn--primary" id="gen" type="button">Make the QR code</button>
      <a class="btn" id="download" href="#" download="calquna-qr.png" style="margin-left:0.5rem;text-decoration:none;">Download the picture</a>
    </p>
    <div style="margin-top:1rem;">
      <canvas id="qr" class="qr-preview" width="256" height="256" role="img" aria-label="Preview of your QR code"></canvas>
    </div>
    <p class="result-note" id="note">Print it, then test it with your own phone before you print fifty.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>What a QR code can hold</h2>
  <p>
    A QR code is just text drawn in a square. A web address opens in the phone’s browser. The
    Wi-Fi format, WIFI:T:WPA;S:name;P:password;; is a convention phones understand, so a guest
    joins by pointing a camera instead of reading a password off the fridge. The contact card
    format, called vCard, drops a name and number straight into the phone’s address book.
    Every code includes spare data, error correction, so it still scans with a quarter of it
    scuffed or covered. This page uses the middle correction level, a fair balance of that
    sturdiness against code density.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions people ask</h2>
  <dl class="faq">
    <dt>Do QR codes expire?</dt>
    <dd>
      Ones made here cannot expire, because the code holds the address itself, not a reference
      to our site. Codes from some services stop working when a subscription lapses, because
      they point at the service first. If a code must work for years, on a sign or a gravestone
      or a book, make sure it holds the address directly, like these do.
    </dd>
    <dt>Can I change the address after printing?</dt>
    <dd>
      No. What is printed is what is encoded. Services that let you change the destination are
      the redirect kind described above, with the expiry risk that comes with them. For
      anything printed, check the address twice.
    </dd>
    <dt>How small can I print it?</dt>
    <dd>
      Keep it at least 2 cm across for a phone at arm’s length, and bigger the further away
      the scanner stands. Contrast matters more than size: dark squares on a light background,
      never the reverse, and keep the quiet white border around the code intact.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="meta">Method: QR encoding at error correction level M, drawn locally with an open source library. Page last checked 13 November 2026.</p>

  <script>
    import QRCode from 'qrcode';

    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
    const canvas = $('qr');

    function payload() {
      const kind = $('kind').value;
      if (kind === 'wifi') {
        const esc = (s) => s.replace(/([\\;,:"'])/g, '\\$1');
        const sec = $('security').value;
        const pass = sec === 'nopass' ? '' : ';P:' + esc($('wifipass').value);
        return 'WIFI:T:' + sec + ';S:' + esc($('ssid').value) + pass + ';;';
      }
      if (kind === 'vcard') {
        return [
          'BEGIN:VCARD',
          'VERSION:3.0',
          'FN:' + $('vc-name').value,
          'ORG:' + $('vc-org').value,
          'TEL;TYPE=CELL:' + $('vc-phone').value,
          'EMAIL:' + $('vc-email').value,
          'END:VCARD',
        ].join('\n');
      }
      return $('url').value || ' ';
    }

    async function generate() {
      const size = parseInt($('size').value, 10);
      try {
        await QRCode.toCanvas(canvas, payload(), { width: size, errorCorrectionLevel: 'M', margin: 2 });
        canvas.style.width = '256px';
        canvas.style.height = '256px';
        $('download').href = canvas.toDataURL('image/png');
        $('note').textContent = 'Ready. The preview is shrunk to fit the page; the download is the full size you picked. Test it with your own phone before you print fifty.';
      } catch {
        $('note').textContent = 'That text is too long for one QR code. Shorten it and try again.';
      }
    }

    $('kind').addEventListener('change', () => {
      const k = $('kind').value;
      $('fields-url').hidden = k !== 'url';
      $('fields-wifi').hidden = k !== 'wifi';
      $('fields-vcard').hidden = k !== 'vcard';
      generate();
    });
    $('gen').addEventListener('click', generate);
    document.querySelectorAll('input, select').forEach((el) => el.addEventListener('input', generate));
    generate();
  </script>
</Base>
